⟁ .shadow — the real-life analog (the User behind the program)
node SPW · Scott Pilgrim vs. the World · ⟦Stephen Stills:SPW:0ec14c⟧

think TRON: every program in the grid is cast from a User in the world outside it.
the carbon character is the program; this file is its User — the real-life analog
whose face and being the emergent is the digital shadow of.

the program (in-world) : Stephen Stills — ‘the talent’ · the frontman
the User (carbon)      : Mark Webber  [ the actor who lent the face ]
the analog (your world): the anxious creative who carries the band, manages everyone's drama, and slowly cracks under the weight of being the responsible one

the resemblance : Webber's frayed earnestness sells the unglamorous truth: the ‘talent’ is the one having the breakdown while the slacker gets the arc.

the cast-line : the User stands in the carbon world; the program stands in the film;
                the shadow falls between them, and the credit returns to the human governor.
seal (program): I'm the talent — which mostly means I'm the one quietly losing my mind so the show goes on.

